  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't build or run it in a browser, so none of it has been checked visually.\n\n- **Island:** a procedural low-poly terrain with per-face normals and vertex colours by height (sand, grass, rock, snow). Instanced low-poly pine trees and rocks sit on it.\n- **Water:** a 240 m grid with a custom GLSL material. Three sine waves displace it, and the fragment shader uses faceted normals, a fresnel mix with the sky colour, a sun or moon glint, and a fade to the horizon colour. Wave time, light direction, light colour, sky colour and ambient level are updated every frame.\n- **Sky and lights:** a 20-second day/night cycle moves the sun and moon, and `sky.preetham` follows through `atmosphere.setSky`, with stars at night. The sun's colour shifts warmer near the horizon. A hemisphere light stays on at all times, and a bluish moonlight takes over at night, so the scene is never black.\n- **Camera:** an orbit camera at about 40 m distance and 14 m height frames the whole island. It auto-rotates slowly.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nThe light intensity changes use `setLight?.()`. I couldn't confirm in `node_modules` that `setLight` is implemented. If it isn't, the sun and moon still toggle on and off by elevation, and the hemisphere light stays at its initial 0.9 intensity.\n\n",
